<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tulip Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2005</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tulip Revolution was a wave of protests in Kyrgyzstan in March 2005 that overthrew President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/askar-akayev">Askar Akayev</a>. Triggered by disputed parliamentary elections, it began in the south, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalal-abad">Jalal-Abad</a> and Osh, and culminated in the storming of the presidential offices in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishkek">Bishkek</a> on 24 March. Akayev fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and resigned, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurmanbek-bakiyev">Kurmanbek Bakiyev</a> became president, though he was himself ousted in a further uprising in 2010.</p></div>
